\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God of my salvation, hear,
\par And help me to believe;
\par Simply do I now draw near,
\par Thy blessing to receive:
\par Full of sin, alas! I am,
\par But to Thy wounds for refuge flee:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Friend of sinners, spotleess Lamb,
\par Thy blood was shed for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\b0 
\par \cf0\ulnone 2. Standing now as newly slain,
\par To Thee I lift mine eye;
\par Balm of all my grief and pain,
\par Thy grace is always nigh:
\par Now as yesterday the same
\par Thou art, and wilt for ever be:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Friend of sinners, spotleess Lamb,
\par Thy blood was shed for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Nothing have I, Lord, to pay,
\par Nor can Thy grace procure;
\par Empty send me not away,
\par For I, Thou know'st, am poor:
\par Dust and ashes is my name,
\par My all is sin and misery:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Friend of sinners, spotleess Lamb,
\par Thy blood was shed for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. No good word, or work, or thought
\par Bring I to gain Thy grace;
\par Pardon I accept unbought,
\par Thine offer I embrace,
\par Coming, as at first I came,
\par To take, and not bestow on Thee:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Friend of sinners, spotleess Lamb,
\par Thy blood was shed for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Saviour, from Thy wounded side
\par I never will depart;
\par Here will I my spirit hide
\par When I am pure in heart:
\par Till my place above I claim,
\par This only shall be all my plea:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Friend of sinners, spotleess Lamb,
\par Thy blood was shed for me.
\par \cf1\ul\b\f1 
\par 
\par }

